## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Ba: Giải thích khái niệm

**Chủ đề: vì sao "nhắc tôi lúc 12 giờ" là bài toán khó.**

> *"I spent this morning on something that sounds trivial: remind me at noon.*
> *The question is what you store. If you store the string 'twelve o'clock' you don't know twelve o'clock where. If you store a UTC timestamp, then the user flies to Tokyo and still gets reminded on Vietnam time. So you store the wall clock time plus the IANA zone name, and you resolve to UTC at send time.*
> *And it has to be the zone name, not the offset. Offsets change — daylight saving moves them twice a year. The zone name is stable.*
> *The general rule I ended up with: for something that already happened, store an absolute instant. For something that should happen at a local time in the future, store the clock time and the zone.*
> *The other half was quiet hours, and the case everyone gets wrong first is a window that crosses midnight — ten at night to seven in the morning. A naive between-check returns false for the entire window. I wrote a test for that before I wrote the code.*
> *And every reminder job has an idempotency key, because if the dispatcher runs twice the user gets notified twice, and that's how you get uninstalled."*

**5 từ mới:**

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `wall clock time` | giờ trên đồng hồ treo tường | *Store the wall clock time plus the zone.* |
| `resolve to UTC` | quy về giờ UTC | *You resolve to UTC at send time.* |
| `daylight saving` | giờ mùa hè | *Daylight saving moves offsets twice a year.* |
| `absolute instant` | thời điểm tuyệt đối | *For something that happened, store an absolute instant.* |
| `cross midnight` | vắt qua nửa đêm | *A window that crosses midnight.* |

